["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>One 12 gauge does ducks with steel and grouse and quail. Know its parts, action, chokes and plug.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 320\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Parts of a pump or semi auto shotgun, side view. From the back: recoil pad, stock, grip, trigger and trigger guard with the safety button, receiver with the ejection port, fore end, magazine tube under the barrel, barrel with the rib on top, bead sight and choke tube at the muzzle.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Parts of your shotgun</text>\n  <!-- stock -->\n  <path d=\"M26 138 L120 146 L124 168 L104 170 L26 196 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"16\" y=\"136\" width=\"12\" height=\"62\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <!-- receiver -->\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"136\" width=\"60\" height=\"32\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"140\" y=\"144\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <!-- trigger guard -->\n  <path d=\"M128 168 Q 132 192 160 188 L164 168\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M146 168 q -2 10 4 14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"172\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <!-- barrel, rib, mag tube, fore end -->\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"138\" width=\"200\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"134\" width=\"196\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"370\" y=\"137\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"132\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"150\" width=\"150\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <rect x=\"330\" y=\"149\" width=\"10\" height=\"12\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"196\" y=\"148\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <!-- leaders top -->\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\">\n    <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"66\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"96\"/><line x1=\"152\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"66\"/>\n    <line x1=\"290\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"96\"/><line x1=\"372\" y1=\"129\" x2=\"372\" y2=\"66\"/>\n    <line x1=\"22\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"22\" y2=\"236\"/><line x1=\"148\" y1=\"182\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"276\"/><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"175\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"236\"/>\n    <line x1=\"240\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"276\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"236\"/><line x1=\"380\" y1=\"149\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"276\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"60\">Stock</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"90\">Receiver</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"60\">Ejection port</text>\n    <text x=\"290\" y=\"90\">Rib</text><text x=\"364\" y=\"60\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Bead</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"252\" text-anchor=\"start\">Recoil pad</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"292\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Trigger</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"252\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Safety</text>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"292\">Fore end</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"252\">Magazine tube</text><text x=\"364\" y=\"292\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Choke</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pump: you slide the fore end. Semi auto: the gun cycles.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>One <strong>12 gauge</strong>, <strong>3 inch chamber</strong>, screw in chokes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>A <strong>gas semi auto</strong> is softest with heavy steel loads <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: budget and the full short answer</summary><ul><li>You need <strong>one 12 gauge</strong> with a <strong>3 inch chamber</strong> and screw in chokes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>That gun covers ducks with steel and upland birds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>A <strong>gas semi auto</strong> is the softest shooting choice with heavy steel loads <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Budget: entry about $420 to $900, mid about $850 to $1,870, premium about $1,950 to $2,900 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Price checked 2026-10-01.</li><li>Prices are in CAD (Canadian dollars), from search previews of retailer pages. Verify at checkout.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four shotgun actions. Pump: cheapest and simple, most kick. Gas semi auto: softest kick, keep the gas system clean. Inertia semi auto: runs clean in cold, sharper kick. Over under: two barrels, two shots only, check the steel rating.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"46\" width=\"120\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"54\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n    <path d=\"M110 62 h26 m-8 -6 l8 6 l-8 6 M40 62 h-0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"94\">+ Cheapest, simple</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"114\">+ Cycles any load</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"134\" fill=\"#c0392b\">− Most kick</text>\n    <rect x=\"204\" y=\"8\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".15\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <text x=\"216\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gas semi auto</text>\n    <rect x=\"216\" y=\"46\" width=\"120\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><rect x=\"236\" y=\"56\" width=\"70\" height=\"6\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/>\n    <g fill=\"#4a7fb0\"><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"52\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"58\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"278\" cy=\"59\" r=\"3\"/></g>\n    <text x=\"216\" y=\"94\">+ Softest kick</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"114\">+ Best with 3 in steel</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"134\" fill=\"#c0392b\">− Keep gas clean</text>\n    <rect x=\"8\" y=\"154\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\">Inertia semi auto</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"192\" width=\"120\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><path d=\"M30 206 l6 -6 l6 6 l6 -6 l6 6 l6 -6 l6 6\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"240\">+ Runs clean, cold</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"260\" fill=\"#c0392b\">− Sharper kick</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"280\" fill=\"#c0392b\">− Light loads may jam</text>\n    <rect x=\"204\" y=\"154\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"216\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\">Over/under</text>\n    <rect x=\"216\" y=\"190\" width=\"120\" height=\"7\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><rect x=\"216\" y=\"199\" width=\"120\" height=\"7\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/>\n    <text x=\"216\" y=\"240\">+ 2 chokes, easy check</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"260\" fill=\"#c0392b\">− 2 shots only</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"280\" fill=\"#c0392b\">− Check steel rating</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"382\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">My lean</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Pump kicks most. Gas semi auto kicks least <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full table</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Pros</th><th>Cons</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pump</td><td>Cheapest, simple, cycles any load</td><td>Most felt recoil. Beginners short stroke it under stress</td></tr><tr><td>Gas semi auto</td><td>Softest recoil. Best with 3 inch steel</td><td>More parts to clean. Needs the gas system kept clean</td></tr><tr><td>Inertia semi auto</td><td>Runs clean, reliable in cold</td><td>Sharper recoil. Light target loads may not cycle</td></tr><tr><td>Over/under</td><td>2 barrels, 2 chokes, very safe to check open</td><td>2 shots only. Many are not rated for steel. Costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Pump: reliable and cheap, but kicks hardest <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Gas semi auto: spreads recoil, so 3 inch steel feels softer <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Inertia semi auto: stays clean and runs in cold weather <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Over/under: weak as a one gun for ducks plus upland, check steel rating <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 3 inch chamber fires 2 and three quarter inch and 3 inch shells. A 3 and a half inch shell does not fit and adds kick for little gain. Barrel: 28 inch is a good one gun choice, 26 inch swings faster in thick timber.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12 gauge, 3 inch chamber</text>\n  <rect x=\"96\" y=\"40\" width=\"114\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".12\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"153\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 in chamber</text>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"96\" y=\"70\" width=\"14\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"72\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"88\">2 3/4 in</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"88\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓ fits</text>\n    <rect x=\"96\" y=\"104\" width=\"14\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"106\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"122\">3 in</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"122\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓ fits</text>\n    <rect x=\"96\" y=\"138\" width=\"14\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"140\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"156\">3 1/2 in</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"156\" fill=\"#c0392b\">✗ too long</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Barrel length</text>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"216\" width=\"260\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"226\" font-weight=\"bold\">28 in: one gun</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"250\" width=\"242\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><text x=\"272\" y=\"260\" font-weight=\"bold\">26 in: timber</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Synthetic stock, coated finish for rain (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>3 inch chamber fires 2 3/4 and 3 inch shells <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. 28 inch barrel for one gun <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: 20 gauge, 3 1/2 inch, finish</summary><ul><li><strong>Gauge:</strong> 12 gauge has the widest choice of steel loads in every shop <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.<ul><li>20 gauge kicks less but steel loads are weaker for ducks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Chamber:</strong> 3 inch is enough. It fires 2 3/4 inch and 3 inch shells <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.<ul><li>3 1/2 inch adds recoil and cost for little gain on ducks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Barrel:</strong> 28 inch is a good compromise for one gun <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.<ul><li>26 inch swings faster in thick grouse timber <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Finish:</strong> synthetic stock and a coated or camo finish for rain and salt (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: two shot clouds leave the muzzle and fly to a 76 centimetre circle at 37 metres. The Improved Cylinder cloud spreads wide and fills the circle loosely. The Modified cloud stays tighter and denser.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shot spreads as it flies</text>\n  <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"58\">IC</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"210\">M</text></g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"234\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"90\" r=\"46\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"240\" r=\"46\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dashed ring: 76 cm (30 in) at 37 m (40 yd)</text>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"44 90;330 90\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <g fill=\"#e8590c\">\n      <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"0.12;1\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-30\" cy=\"-20\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"-24\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-40\" cy=\"10\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"14\" r=\"3\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"34\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"38\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"-40\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-20\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"3\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-52\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"44\" cy=\"36\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-44\" cy=\"38\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"18\" r=\"3\"/>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"44 240;330 240\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <g fill=\"#e8590c\">\n      <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"0.12;1\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-18\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-24\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"9\" r=\"3\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"-7\" cy=\"20\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"23\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-5\" cy=\"-24\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-1\" r=\"3\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"-5\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-31\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"-26\" cy=\"23\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"11\" r=\"3\"/>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <text x=\"180\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wide: about 50%</text>\n    <text x=\"180\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tighter: about 60%</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Tighter choke, tighter pattern. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>A <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Choke\">Choke</button> squeezes the shot at the muzzle <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>With steel: <strong>nothing tighter than Modified</strong> unless marked steel safe <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how chokes work, numbers</summary><ul><li>A choke is a short tube at the muzzle. It squeezes the shot to control spread <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Tighter choke means a smaller, denser pattern at range <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Steel is hard. It does not squeeze like lead. Tight chokes can damage the choke or barrel <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Rule of thumb: <strong>nothing tighter than Modified with steel</strong> unless the choke says steel safe <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>IC (Improved Cylinder) for ducks over decoys and close grouse. M (Modified) for longer passing ducks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Squeeze in a 12 gauge: IC about 0.25 mm (0.010 in), M about 0.5 mm (0.020 in) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Full about 0.76 to 1 mm (0.030 to 0.040 in). Makers differ <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Classic benchmark at 37 m (40 yd): Cylinder 40%, IC 50%, M 60%, Full 70% of pellets inside a 76 cm (30 in) circle <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>You test your own gun on paper in Session 5 (patterning).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 560\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"560\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chokes: spread at 37 m (40 yd)</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dashed ring = 76 cm (30 in) circle</text>\n\n  <!-- Cylinder -->\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Cylinder</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">0 squeeze</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 40% in ring</text>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"115\" r=\"56\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.45\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"115\" r=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"296\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Steel OK</text>\n\n  <!-- IC -->\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">IC</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Improved Cylinder</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 0.25 mm</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 50% in ring</text>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"240\" r=\"49\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.55\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"240\" r=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"296\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Steel OK</text>\n\n  <!-- Modified -->\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">M (Modified)</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"370\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 0.5 mm</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"390\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 60% in ring</text>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"365\" r=\"42\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.7\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"365\" r=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"296\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Steel</text>\n  <text x=\"296\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">OK *</text>\n\n  <!-- Full -->\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"475\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Full</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"495\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 0.8 to 1 mm</text>\n  <text x=\"15\" y=\"515\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 70% in ring</text>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"490\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" fill-opacity=\"0.7\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"490\" r=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"296\" y=\"485\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">NO</text>\n  <text x=\"296\" y=\"505\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">unless</text>\n  <text x=\"296\" y=\"521\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">marked</text>\n\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"548\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">General guide only. * Most makers. Your manual wins.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Choke ladder from open to tight: Cylinder, Improved Cylinder and Modified are fine with steel shot. Improved Modified, Full and Extra Full are not, unless the tube is marked steel safe. Your gun's manual wins.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Steel shot: which chokes?</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\">\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"63\" fill=\"#fff\">Cylinder</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"80\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"103\" fill=\"#fff\">Improved Cylinder</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"120\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"143\" fill=\"#fff\">Modified</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"164\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\" opacity=\".8\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"187\" fill=\"#fff\">Improved Modified</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"204\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\" opacity=\".8\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"227\" fill=\"#fff\">Full</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"244\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\" opacity=\".8\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"267\" fill=\"#fff\">Extra Full, turkey</text>\n  </g>\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"159\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"159\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\">\n    <text x=\"236\" y=\"86\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">✓ Steel OK</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">IC: decoys, grouse</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">M: passing ducks</text>\n    <text x=\"236\" y=\"204\" fill=\"#c0392b\">✗ Not with steel</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">unless marked</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">steel safe</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Open</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Tight</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Your gun's manual wins</strong> (Tip). Learn the notches or stamps on your tubes (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what each maker says</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Brand</th><th>What the maker says about steel (general)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Benelli</td><td>No tighter than Modified with steel <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Beretta</td><td>Cylinder, IC, Modified are steel ok. Not Full or Improved Modified <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Browning (Invector Plus)</td><td>Accepts factory steel. Not Full or Extra Full with steel <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Stoeger</td><td>IC and Modified ok. XFT (Extra Full Turkey) not for steel <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mossberg</td><td>Not with X Full or XX Full tubes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Remington</td><td>Full only if the tube says \"for steel or lead shot\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Franchi, Winchester</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> in the owner's manual</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>IC means Improved Cylinder.</li><li>These are general summaries of maker guidance. <strong>Your gun's manual wins</strong> (Tip).</li><li>Choke tubes are often stamped or notched. Learn your marks before the hunt (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gun fit. Length of pull is measured from the trigger to the end of the stock, about 14 to 14.75 inches for most adults. Eyes shut test: mount the gun, open your eyes, you should look straight down the rib at the bead.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Does it fit you?</text>\n  <path d=\"M30 60 L190 72 L194 98 L170 100 L30 128 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"58\" width=\"12\" height=\"72\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"190\" y=\"64\" width=\"60\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"250\" y=\"66\" width=\"130\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/>\n  <path d=\"M200 94 q 4 14 16 14\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"206\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M30 144 l-10 6 l10 6 M196 144 l10 6 l-10 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"113\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Length of pull</text>\n  <text x=\"113\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">most adults 14 to 14.75 in</text>\n  <!-- eye test -->\n  <ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"250\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"66\" cy=\"250\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <line x1=\"92\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"346\" cy=\"246\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"220\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Eyes shut, mount, open</text>\n  <text x=\"220\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You see straight down the rib (Tip)</text>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Try it on</text>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in your jacket</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Try guns on <strong>in your hunting jacket</strong> (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: length of pull and shims</summary><ul><li>LOP (length of pull) is trigger to the end of the stock. Most adults need about 14 to 14.75 inches <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>A winter jacket makes the stock feel longer. Try guns on <strong>in your hunting jacket</strong> (Tip).</li><li>Beretta A300 Ultima: about 13.8 inch stock plus 2 spacers to lengthen it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Quick test: mount the gun with eyes shut, open them. You should look straight down the rib (Tip).</li><li>Many semi autos come with shims to change drop and cast. Ask the shop to set it (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Magazine plug. A one piece plug fills most of the magazine tube. With the plug in, the magazine holds 2 shells and the chamber holds 1, for 3 total. That is the limit for ducks and geese. BC also needs the plug for quail and grouse.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The plug: 3 shells max</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cutaway, muzzle to the right</text>\n  <!-- receiver and chamber -->\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"70\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"76\" width=\"280\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"104\" y=\"79\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"135\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chamber: 1</text>\n  <!-- mag tube -->\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"110\" width=\"280\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"104\" y=\"114\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"114\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <path d=\"M224 122 l8 -6 l8 12 l8 -12 l8 12 l8 -6\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <rect x=\"264\" y=\"113\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Plug</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Magazine: 2</text>\n  <g font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"180\" width=\"170\" height=\"100\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n    <text x=\"105\" y=\"208\" fill=\"#fff\">Ducks, geese</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\">3 total</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">federal law</text>\n    <rect x=\"210\" y=\"180\" width=\"170\" height=\"100\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <text x=\"295\" y=\"208\" fill=\"#fff\">Grouse, quail</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"240\" fill=\"#fff\">Plug in too</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">magazine 2 max, BC</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ducks and geese: <strong>3 shells max</strong>, one piece plug <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Quail and grouse in BC: plug in too, magazine 2 max <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the exact law and non toxic shot</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>For migratory birds (ducks, geese), the shotgun may hold <strong>no more than 3 shells</strong> in magazine and chamber combined <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. The <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Magazine plug\">Magazine plug</button> must be one piece and removable only by taking the gun apart <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. A detachable magazine may hold no more than 2 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</p></aside><ul><li>Most new semi autos and pumps ship with the plug installed. Check before every duck hunt (Tip).</li><li>Quail and grouse too: in BC a pump, semi auto or other repeating shotgun needs a plug so the magazine holds no more than 2 shells <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Leave it in all season (Tip).</li><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Non toxic shot\">Non toxic shot</button> (steel, bismuth, tungsten, tin) is required for ducks, geese, coots and snipe <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Pigeons and doves are the exception <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"s3-used\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:0\"><span>Ask the seller to show it is unloaded. Check it yourself</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:1\"><span>Look through the bore from both ends: no rust, pits or bulges</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:2\"><span>Choke tubes come out by hand or with the wrench, not seized</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:3\"><span>Choke wrench and a set of tubes come with it</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:4\"><span>Work the action 10 times: smooth, no grinding</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:5\"><span>Gas gun: check piston and O ring are clean and present</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:6\"><span>Inertia gun: ask about the recoil spring</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:7\"><span>Plug is present (needed for all bird hunting)</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:8\"><span>Stock and recoil pad not cracked</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:9\"><span>Serial number present and readable</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s3-used:10\"><span>Show your PAL (Possession and Acquisition Licence). Seller checks it with the RCMP (Royal Canadian Mounted Police)</span></label></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: private sale</summary><ul><li>For a private sale, the seller must confirm your PAL with the RCMP and get a reference number <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Exact steps: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Action</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Stoeger P3000</td><td>Pump</td><td>$417 to $575</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mossberg 500 Field</td><td>Pump</td><td>$639.99</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Benelli SuperNova</td><td>Pump</td><td>about $700 to $935</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Stoeger M3000</td><td>Inertia semi auto</td><td>$725 to $890</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mossberg 835 Waterfowl</td><td>Pump, 3 1/2 inch</td><td>$809.99</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li></ul>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Action</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Stoeger M3500</td><td>Inertia semi auto</td><td>$849.99 to $1,095</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Beretta A300 Outlander</td><td>Gas semi auto</td><td>$1,117 to $1,349</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Beretta A300 Ultima</td><td>Gas semi auto</td><td>$1,400 to $1,525</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Winchester SX4 Waterfowl</td><td>Gas semi auto</td><td>$1,367 to $1,570</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Browning Silver Field</td><td>Gas semi auto</td><td>$1,630 to $1,865</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li></ul>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Action</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Browning Maxus II</td><td>Gas semi auto</td><td>$1,950 to $2,850</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Benelli SBE3</td><td>Inertia semi auto</td><td>$2,295 to $2,900</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Beretta A400 Xtreme Plus</td><td>Gas semi auto</td><td>$2,515 to $2,760</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Benelli Montefeltro Silver</td><td>Inertia semi auto</td><td>$2,595 to $2,710</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Premium buys softer recoil and finish, not more ducks (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: price note</summary><ul><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li><li>Premium buys softer recoil, better finish and resale. It does not buy more ducks (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>A <strong>Beretta A300</strong>, gas semi auto, 12 gauge, 3 inch, 28 inch barrel. About $1,120 to $1,525. Outlander if it fits, Ultima if you need the adjustable stock. Try the SX4 and M3000 side by side too.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Buy the gun that fits, not the gun that wins the magazine test.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Steel through a Full choke not marked steel safe.</li><li>Pulling the plug for quail. BC law needs it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Fitting the gun in a T shirt, hunting in a thick jacket.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>At the shop: wear your hunting jacket, mount 3 guns 10 times each, ask which chokes come in the box.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Plug and shot rules read directly in federal and BC law <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Gear, chokes and prices: secondary sources (65 to 80%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-2022-105/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022 (SOR/2022-105), full text</a>, read directly, current to 2026-09-21: s. 37 (3 shells, one piece plug, detachable magazine), s. 38 (non toxic shot, pigeon and dove exceptions). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, read directly. Printed p. 12 (shotgun plug), p. 13 (note 4, shot ban notice). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/96488_01\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildlife Act, RSBC 1996 c. 488</a>, s. 26(1)(h) (plug rule for pump, repeating and auto loading shotguns), read directly, current to 22 September 2026. Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Benelli, Beretta, Browning, Remington steel and choke guidance via <a href=\"https://www.shotgunworld.com/threads/which-choke-for-steel-shot.7870/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">shotgunworld.com</a> and <a href=\"https://www.rem870.com/2012/05/06/shotgun-chokes-explained-cylinder-improved-cylinder-modified-full/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">rem870.com</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (75%, secondary)</li><li>Choke constriction: <a href=\"https://shotgunweb.com/chokes/constriction-chart\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">shotgunweb.com constriction chart</a> and <a href=\"https://www.themeateater.com/hunt/firearm-hunting/everything-you-need-to-know-about-shotgun-choke-tubes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TheMeatEater choke guide</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>Pattern percentages: <a href=\"https://www.nrafamily.org/content/how-to-pattern-a-shotgun/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NRA Family, how to pattern a shotgun</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (70%, search preview)</li><li>Action pros and cons: Field and Stream, Impact Guns, Ducks Unlimited, via Hunt Mentor gear research 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>Retail prices: search previews of Canadian retailer pages, price checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>Note: check your own gun's manual for choke and steel rules.</li></ul></details>"]